  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the neighbourhood of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, we know,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cot</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Now,&nbsp;for the neighbourhood of <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow>